---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
const description = 'Privacy policies for Dudley Development apps.';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description={description} path="/privacy/">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/')}>← Home</a>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Effective date: September 7, 2026 · One policy per app — pick yours below.</p>

      <p>
        {LEGAL_NAME} makes several separate apps, and they don't all collect the same things, so there
        isn't one policy that's accurate for all of them. Read the policy for the app you actually use —
        the table below is a quick summary, and each app's own page has the full detail. A few things are
        true everywhere: we never sell your personal data, we don't share data across our own apps to
        build a profile of you, none of our apps are directed at children, and any usage analytics we run
        ourselves is anonymous and disclosed on the app's page below. Some free apps show ads through
        Google AdMob, which is disclosed per app, including whether the ad requests are personalized and
        whether Apple's tracking permission is involved.
      </p>

      <h2>Quick comparison</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll" style="overflow-x:auto; margin:1rem 0;">
        <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:0.92rem;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px 10px 6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #333);">App</th>
              <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #333);">Crash reports</th>
              <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #333);">Usage analytics</th>
              <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #333);">Ads</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Powell Prowl: Rate Chase</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">No</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">No</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Google AdMob, with an ATT prompt (personalized unless you decline)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">VibeRater Social</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Yes (Sentry)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Yes (PostHog, pseudonymous; off in Private mode)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Google AdMob, non-personalized, no ATT prompt</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Table Talk: Conversation Cards</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Yes (Sentry, from v1.1.1)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Yes (PostHog, on by default, opt-out in Settings, from v1.1.1)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Google AdMob, non-personalized, no ATT prompt</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">EconByte: Daily Economics</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Off by default (Settings opt-in)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Off by default (Settings opt-in)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Google AdMob, non-personalized, no ATT prompt</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Last Human: Dodge the Bots</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Yes (Sentry)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Yes (PostHog, on by default, opt-out in Settings)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border, #222);">Google AdMob, non-personalized, no ATT prompt, plus an optional rewarded ad to continue a run</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0;">Beat the Dealer: Card Counting</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px;">Yes when configured (Sentry)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px;">Opt-in only (PostHog, off until Enable Optional Analytics)</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px;">Google AdMob, non-personalized, no ATT prompt; no ads in EEA/UK/CH</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <ul class="policy-list">
        <li>
          <a class="row" href={rel('/privacy/monetary-policy-independence-day')}>
            <img src={rel('/assets/powell-prowl-icon.png')} alt="Powell Prowl: Rate Chase app icon" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="meta"><b>Powell Prowl: Rate Chase</b><span>Privacy policy</span></span>
            <span class="chev">→</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="row" href={rel('/privacy/vibe-rater')}>
            <img src={rel('/assets/vibe-rater-icon.png')} alt="VibeRater Social app icon" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="meta"><b>VibeRater Social</b><span>Privacy policy</span></span>
            <span class="chev">→</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="row" href={rel('/privacy/table-talk')}>
            <img src={rel('/assets/table-talk-icon.png')} alt="Table Talk app icon" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="meta"><b>Table Talk: Conversation Cards</b><span>Privacy policy</span></span>
            <span class="chev">→</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="row" href={rel('/privacy/econbyte')}>
            <img src={rel('/assets/econbyte-icon.png')} alt="EconByte app icon" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="meta"><b>EconByte: Daily Economics</b><span>Privacy policy</span></span>
            <span class="chev">→</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="row" href={rel('/privacy/last-human')}>
            <img src={rel('/assets/last-human-icon.png')} alt="Last Human app icon" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="meta"><b>Last Human: Dodge the Bots</b><span>Privacy policy</span></span>
            <span class="chev">→</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="row" href={rel('/privacy/beat-the-dealer')}>
            <img src={rel('/assets/beat-the-dealer-icon.png')} alt="Beat the Dealer: Card Counting app icon" width="44" height="44" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="meta"><b>Beat the Dealer: Card Counting</b><span>Privacy policy</span></span>
            <span class="chev">→</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What's true across every Dudley app</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>{LEGAL_NAME} is the developer of every app listed here. We are not a data broker and we do not sell personal data.</li>
        <li>None of our apps use your data from one Dudley app to target or personalize another.</li>
        <li>None of our apps are directed at children, and none knowingly collect data from anyone under 13 (VibeRater requires users to be at least 16).</li>
        <li>Where an app runs its own crash reporting or usage analytics, it is disclosed on that app's page, uses a random per-install or per-account identifier rather than your name or contact details, and is never used to serve ads.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about any app, or a data request? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
